{"recordId":"tier-c3c3-family-1015647582cbd6a9","eventType":"tier-c3c3-quadriliteral-root-adjudication","contractId":"quranic-word-tree-authoring","contractVersion":"1.3.9","scope":{"familyKey":"lexical|قطمر|قطمير|noun/pronoun","occurrences":["word:35:13:28"],"tier":"C3-C3","track":"QUADRILITERAL"},"status":"blocked","reviewedAt":"2026-10-22T22:09:58.058Z","checks":["contract-loaded","c3c3-quadriliteral-scope-22-families","c3c3-occurrence-scope-27","every-occurrence-inspected","current-form-first","canonical-four-radical-root-recorded","four-radical-equality-check","quadriliteral-primary-track-ownership","same-quadriliteral-root-forms-reviewed","triliteral-cross-root-candidates-rejected","generated-unattested-forms-rejected","shell-case-pronoun-and-padding-rejected","semantic-development-translated-honestly","provenance-recorded","decision-recorded"],"evidence":["This is a highly lexicalised technical noun in the Qur’anic usage. The standard five-row family would require speculative verbs or participles; the correct product treatment is a dedicated lexicalised-noun representation.","Generated قَطْمَرَ, يُقَطْمِرُ, قَطْمَرَةٌ and participles were rejected because no approved authoritative evidence established them for this root.","Case variation in قِطْمِيرٍ is not morphology.","A reviewed model for lexicalised quadriliteral nouns that displays the root and stable meaning without implying a productive paradigm."],"decision":"MODEL-ISSUE","root":"قطمر","lemmaOrCurrentForm":"قِطْمِير","category":"C3-C3 quadriliteral root","humanExpertReviewRequired":true}
